<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Mandurah & Peel takes in four councils: the City of Mandurah and the Shires of Murray, Serpentine-Jarrahdale and Waroona. It's growing fast, too. ABS estimates for June 2025 put Mandurah at 106,827 people, and Serpentine-Jarrahdale grew 4.5% in a single year. More houses means more owners staring at a crack above the laundry door, or wondering whether the wall between the kitchen and lounge can come out.</p><p>Kings Park Structural Co is a referral service, not an engineering firm. We pass your enquiry to an independent structural engineering firm, which quotes you and contracts with you directly. Sometimes the honest answer on the first call is that you don't need an engineer at all, and it's better to hear that before you pay anyone. <strong>Call now on (08) 5550 6237.</strong></p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Do in Mandurah & Peel</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">Services for Mandurah & Peel Properties</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #ECE5D8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#15191E;margin:0 0 8px;">Wall removal and beam design</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">WA is the only state where most detached houses are brick, and in a double-brick house some internal walls usually hold up ceilings and roof. The engineer who quotes your job works out whether yours is one of them and, if it is, designs the beam and supports the permit needs.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #ECE5D8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#15191E;margin:0 0 8px;">Crack and structural inspection reports</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Clay along the Serpentine River swells and shrinks with moisture, while coastal sand is more prone to washing away from a leak. An engineer's report looks at walls, floors, slab and footings and gives you a view on what the cracking means.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #ECE5D8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#15191E;margin:0 0 8px;">Extensions, second storeys and granny flats</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Anything that changes a home's floor area or height needs a building permit in WA, whether it's in Halls Head or Byford. The builder or building surveyor will often want engineering for footings and structure before lodging.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #ECE5D8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Figtree',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#15191E;margin:0 0 8px;">Patio, carport and shed certificates</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A roofed patio isn't a pergola under the WA exemptions, and a freestanding shed only skips a permit if it's 10 m² or less and no more than 2.4 m high, among other conditions. For everything else, the permit application may need an engineer's certificate covering site class and wind.</p>
      </div>
</div>
<style>
